A second attribute of the bible that derives from divine inspiration is the authority of scripture. God has all authority therefore whenever and however he speaks all who hear him are obligated to obey him. The bible claims divine authority in two ways; 
1. Claim of Authority- a. Historical examples- In the days of Moses God encoded his spoken word in written word and his speech carried authority. God's authoritative covenant document that his people are obligated to obey. Jesus frequently appealed to Scripture to justify and explain his actions. Paul believed that God's authoritative word binded New testament believers.
2. Explicit claims- The Bible proves its authority through explicit statements because prophecies were inspired and authorized by God, they form a moral standard. The ongoing authority of Scripture is based on God's authority.

